{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera","id":789857,"title":"Primal Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-20T12:13:21-08:00","id":789857,"title":"Primal Fera","content":"Have any of you every looked at a documentary for dire wolves, the short-faced bear, or the dinosaurs and think &quot;if that were a were-creature it would kick ass&quot;. I mean think of all those A grade super predators that dominated the landscape and only went out because they got a cheap shot from the sky(a big meteor, the ice ages, etc etc.) And tell me they wouldn't be badass in a were-creature fight.<br /> <br /> Well, why wouldn't they have been were-creatures? Ever think it was weird how when mages or garou went umbra diving they'd occasionally find something that was suppose to be extinct a million years ago roaming around like it owned the place(and likely very hungry). Ever Think some Other things may have survived with them?<br /> <br /> What would these &quot;Primal&quot; Were-Creatures be like? how did tghey survive? what powers might such being have?<br /> <br /> Share your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T15:25:25-08:00","id":789951,"title":"","content":"THe Mokole were Dinosaurs, the Khara (bastet tribe) were Sabertooths, and theres no reason that the Short-faced bear wouldn't have be Gurahl since they don't separate based on breed of bear but where they hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T16:00:45-08:00","id":789966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=789951#post789951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe Mokole were Dinosaurs, the Khara (bastet tribe) were Sabertooths, and theres no reason that the Short-faced bear wouldn't have be Gurahl since they don't separate based on breed of bear but where they hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, what I was asking was how these &quot;primal&quot; were-creatures would be different from their smaller weaker brethren. Like for instance a Primal Mokole would already have 1-5 ranks in huge size(depending on dinosaur) without investing any of its trait pool, much higher physical stats, access to a wide range of gifts and rites that have long since been lost, and wouldn't have access to a human form(they didn't exist at the time). That's just where the differences begin, but you get my point<br /> <br /> If dire wolf for instance is considered the apex of wolf evolution, a dire wolf garou then could be conceived to have been the apex among garou as well(the sudden extinction brought on by lack of food could event be attributed to the wyrm wiping out the greatest of gaia's warriors). This could apply to any fera in WOD as well, as every surviving species on earth have a primal ancestor that once surpassed it in every function. <br /> <br /> I was wondering how one would come up with rules for such a creature if it was found today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T18:42:06-08:00","id":790024,"title":"","content":"Well this is a game first and foremost, so I'm not sure why they would be spending 1-5 ranks of huge size without investing any points into the pool for balance reasons. The Shattered Dreams does talk a bit about Dinosaur mokole but it seems like they only get a rank or 2 for free which would only apply to their suchid forms (kinda like how the Ao get armored scales or the Unktehi get venom which are both only 1 rank). Also as for a wide range of gifts and rites that have been lost...that can be true but at the same time think of how many newer gifts and rites could have been invented since their extinction (for example the Gumgan get a lot of gifts that are from the Bunyip like Bloody Minded). <br /> <br /> As for &quot;Apex&quot; of wolf evolution...what makes it the apex? I'd argue it wasn't....as it is no longer around anymore and was geographically rather restricted compared to Canis lupus....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T21:20:36-08:00","id":790080,"title":"","content":"Dire wolves weren't all that much larger than timber wolves. They were also slightly shorter or even in height, being more blocked off and squat, with a heavy, hyena-like build and jaw structure. Very unlike what Garou would be looking for in kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790024#post790024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;Apex&quot; of wolf evolution...what makes it the apex? I'd argue it wasn't....as it is no longer around anymore and was geographically rather restricted compared to Canis lupus....</div> </div> </div> </div>Also because it represents a side branch of coyote evolution and was shit at running, making it more like a shape that Ajaba would grab through Mokole breed-switching tricks than one in the Garou bag. Also, because there is never really an apex to evolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-21-2015, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T22:06:57-08:00","id":790097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790080#post790080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there is never really an apex to evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was what I was really getting at I guess, without quite stating it directly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T08:18:03-08:00","id":790284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790080#post790080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dire wolves weren't all that much larger than timber wolves. They were also slightly shorter or even in height, being more blocked off and squat, with a heavy, hyena-like build and jaw structure. Very unlike what Garou would be looking for in kin.<br /> <br /> Also because it represents a side branch of coyote evolution and was shit at running, making it more like a shape that Ajaba would grab through Mokole breed-switching tricks than one in the Garou bag. Also, because there is never really an apex to evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but they were larger, stronger, of sturdier build and had larger packs with more members than any modern wolf.<br /> <br /> As for the apex evolution thing, Evolution may not have an apex, but some of our extinct ancestors once surpassed us in every facet(with the exception of humans of course, nothing on record has every been smarter than us). The reason most of them went extinct is a very weird fact of nature, the &quot;Biggest and strongest&quot; rarely survive extinction events. Typically when food runs out it's the meek little bunny rabbit that can live off a few blades of grass that survives as opposed to the strong lion that needs a deer a day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790080#post790080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this is a game first and foremost, so I'm not sure why they would be spending 1-5 ranks of huge size without investing any points into the pool for balance reasons. The Shattered Dreams does talk a bit about Dinosaur mokole but it seems like they only get a rank or 2 for free which would only apply to their suchid forms (kinda like how the Ao get armored scales or the Unktehi get venom which are both only 1 rank).</div> </div> </div> </div>And dinosaur mokole only get size in suchid form? That's... incredibly stupid. Considering the fact that would mean a tyrannosaurus rex has to shrink down 5 levels to use its &quot;War&quot; form, that Sounds on par with masters of the art levels of stupid to me. If they also get &quot;Human forms&quot; without having to use a gift like thousand forms, I must say that I don't think they are the same Dinosaur Mokole as existed in the actual dinosaur era.<br /> <br /> This rings too much as balanced for &quot;Player&quot; characters, when the WOD team thinks we'll all be playing dinosaurs by tomorrow if they have any sort of advantage over the the others of it's kind, and decide to balance it mechanically without regards to what would make sense in narrative. As a storyteller that seriously pisses me off because it's like they don't think we're smart enough to know that if a player tries to hand you a character sheet for an abomination or a cyborg dinosaur we should laugh and make them roll a real character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:22:31-08:00","id":790334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790284#post790284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a storyteller that seriously pisses me off because it's like they don't think we're smart enough to know that if a player tries to hand you a character sheet for an abomination or a cyborg dinosaur we should laugh and make them roll a real character.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a storyteller you can do whatever you want. You don't like balanced saurian Mokole? Fine, give them whatever powers you want- it doesn't sound like you are allowing a PC to have it anyway, so who cares?<br /> <br /> As for size limitations related to Suchid... there are other fera whose 'warform' is not as potent as others- arguably the Garou themselves are this way with Hispo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:43:54-08:00","id":790347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790334#post790334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a storyteller you can do whatever you want. You don't like balanced saurian Mokole? Fine, give them whatever powers you want- it doesn't sound like you are allowing a PC to have it anyway, so who cares?<br /> <br /> As for size limitations related to Suchid... there are other fera whose 'warform' is not as potent as others- arguably the Garou themselves are this way with Hispo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, golden rule and all that right? It just infuriates me when the devs restrict narrative in favor of mechanics or vise versa. Some things really shouldn't be &quot;Balanced&quot; for players as it causes things like the notorious &quot;over-balanced&quot; npcs in VTM, where you can have an ancient vampire elder and a five year old neonate with the same number of backgrounds and disciplines because they're &quot;Plot&quot; npcs.<br /> <br /> A game that focus's to much on balance inevitably causes conflict between the narrative and the mechanics, when instead the best stories are told when a storyteller marries the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:00:01-08:00","id":790388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790347#post790347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, golden rule and all that right? It just infuriates me when the devs restrict narrative in favor of mechanics or vise versa. Some things really shouldn't be &quot;Balanced&quot; for players as it causes things like the notorious &quot;over-balanced&quot; npcs in VTM, where you can have an ancient vampire elder and a five year old neonate with the same number of backgrounds and disciplines because they're &quot;Plot&quot; npcs.<br /> <br /> A game that focus's to much on balance inevitably causes conflict between the narrative and the mechanics, when instead the best stories are told when a storyteller marries the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think balance is a good thing, and it isn't mutually exclusive with being able to tell good stories.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't much like the rules presented for playing Dragon-Kinds Mokole, so the simple fix is that if I were to run such a game (or use one as an NPC) I would just ignore those rules and make up my own. Problem solved. But using the Golden rule isn't terribly helpful pertaining to forum discussions.<br /> <br /> On the original topic: if you want to have Were-Dire Wolves, just use the Hispo form stats and call it a day. Possibly give them an addition +1 to a stat or 2 in Crinos if it fits your fancy. Drop Lupus and possibly Homid as well. This solution works just as well for most of the Changers with 5 forms.<br /> <br /> What other &quot;Apex Predators&quot; (not arguing with the decision to call them that) were you thinking of statting out? Garou, Gurahl and Bastet are esily dealt with (with the system above imo) so what other animals did you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T17:29:40-08:00","id":790576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790388#post790388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think balance is a good thing, and it isn't mutually exclusive with being able to tell good stories.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't much like the rules presented for playing Dragon-Kinds Mokole, so the simple fix is that if I were to run such a game (or use one as an NPC) I would just ignore those rules and make up my own. Problem solved. But using the Golden rule isn't terribly helpful pertaining to forum discussions.<br /> <br /> On the original topic: if you want to have Were-Dire Wolves, just use the Hispo form stats and call it a day. Possibly give them an addition +1 to a stat or 2 in Crinos if it fits your fancy. Drop Lupus and possibly Homid as well. This solution works just as well for most of the Changers with 5 forms.<br /> <br /> What other &quot;Apex Predators&quot; (not arguing with the decision to call them that) were you thinking of statting out? Garou, Gurahl and Bastet are esily dealt with (with the system above imo) so what other animals did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones that seemed the most hard to figure stats for would be primal ananasi and surviving insect kin(all of whom would likely be weaver &quot;spinner&quot; creatures, save the moths). Also what &quot;Primal&quot; cousins would the corax or (bat people who's name I can never spell), As the formers ancestors were dinosaurs(already covered) and the latter has no larger relatives that I'm aware of. Not to mention Megalodon rokea, who's cousins have no forms that even come close to that size.<br /> <br /> For handling massive mokole and rokea I was also thinking of of using rule for giant monsters in one of the Hunters supplements, where each success on a strength role destroys a cubic area roughly the size of a small shed. I was also playing with the idea of other &quot;lost&quot; changers or Creating a new changer race via the Kami decendants theory thats been floating around some WTA forums every since the release of WTA: possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T19:16:07-08:00","id":790630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790284#post790284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but they were larger, stronger, of sturdier build and had larger packs with more members than any modern wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means nothing if they kept jumping into tar pits en masse after their prey fell in. Or if you have too many wastefully bulky mouths to feed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the apex evolution thing, Evolution may not have an apex, but some of our extinct ancestors once surpassed us in every facet(with the exception of humans of course, nothing on record has every been smarter than us). The reason most of them went extinct is a very weird fact of nature, the &quot;Biggest and strongest&quot; rarely survive extinction events. Typically when food runs out it's the meek little bunny rabbit that can live off a few blades of grass that survives as opposed to the strong lion that needs a deer a day. </div> </div> </div>And the largest of large dogs tend to have dramatically lowered lifespans, so having a huge body might not work out so well for canids. Canids, who live lives where they have to move all of that damned bulk around frequently, as opposed to cats, which are ambush hunters and don't live in cluttered masses. Also, they apparently don't jump into tar pits after prey with nearly as much frequency.<br /> <br /> So, no need to exclude the middle and go straight to rabbits, a simple reduction of size and family unit size can do wonders for viability. That, or activity levels and group hunting dependence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And dinosaur mokole only get size in suchid form? That's... incredibly stupid. Considering the fact that would mean a tyrannosaurus rex has to shrink down 5 levels to use its &quot;War&quot; form, that Sounds on par with masters of the art levels of stupid to me. If they also get &quot;Human forms&quot; without having to use a gift like thousand forms, I must say that I don't think they are the same Dinosaur Mokole as existed in the actual dinosaur era.<br /> <br /> This rings too much as balanced for &quot;Player&quot; characters, when the WOD team thinks we'll all be playing dinosaurs by tomorrow if they have any sort of advantage over the the others of it's kind, and decide to balance it mechanically without regards to what would make sense in narrative. As a storyteller that seriously pisses me off because it's like they don't think we're smart enough to know that if a player tries to hand you a character sheet for an abomination or a cyborg dinosaur we should laugh and make them roll a real character. </div> </div> </div>The entire Archid customization scheme is all sixes and sevens. It needs to be revised quite heavily in whatever edition that follows, and huge size needs to be addressed as a whole so that if you do plunk down a truly giant critter, it can have mechanical interactions that make more sense than what we presently have. Also, if the developers and writers didn't intend for you to play something literally Godzilla-sized, they should hash that out before writing books depending on one end of that spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T20:51:05-08:00","id":790658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790576#post790576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The ones that seemed the most hard to figure stats for would be primal ananasi and surviving insect kin(all of whom would likely be weaver &quot;spinner&quot; creatures, save the moths).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there should be any &quot;primal ananasi&quot;. So for me, leaving the insect changers as is works out just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790576#post790576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also what &quot;Primal&quot; cousins would the corax or (bat people who's name I can never spell), As the formers ancestors were dinosaurs(already covered) and the latter has no larger relatives that I'm aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the need for the primal ancestors you are looking for. Not every Changer comes from a species that had huge ancestor species.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790576#post790576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not to mention Megalodon rokea, who's cousins have no forms that even come close to that size.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were plenty of normal large sharks around at the time. Again, just use Chasmus stats. Add an additional stat dot or 2 if you feel it necessary. There is no reason general Rokea need Megalodon kin. An not all Megalodons reached 60ft. A large great white Chasmus can already be 45ft long. that would seem to represent the species close enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790576#post790576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For handling massive mokole and rokea I was also thinking of of using rule for giant monsters in one of the Hunters supplements, where each success on a strength role destroys a cubic area roughly the size of a small shed. I was also playing with the idea of other &quot;lost&quot; changers or Creating a new changer race via the Kami decendants theory thats been floating around some WTA forums every since the release of WTA: possessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I just don't see the need. I do agree though that the Huge Size Archid trait doesn't work as intended without house rules. I have notes somewhere for what I did with it. Something along the lines of each additional Huge Size costing a cumulative Gnosis investment and adding cumulative bonuses to Strength and Stamina.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T21:47:33-08:00","id":790677,"title":"","content":"I would advise against using Hispo for a hypothetical dire wolf form's mechanics, since it's a wolf the size of a horse. Just take off all of the Lupus Dex bonus and add one to Strength; its running speed should be down around Crinos, too. Bite damage mods would increase, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790658#post790658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the need for the primal ancestors you are looking for. Not every Changer comes from a species that had huge ancestor species.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in many cases, the &quot;ancestors&quot; cited aren't. Dire wolves were distant cousins to wolves at best, not their progenitors. Megalodon was a kind of a latecomer (but might have been an ancestor to the modern sand-tiger shark, under the <i>Carcharocles</i> hypothesis). Sabertooth cats didn't beget modern cats, big or small. It might work for the Mokole, given the size of <i>Deinosuchus</i>, but for other changers, their animal kin didn't really have remarkably huge progenitors. Giant Protoype Creatures are a thing from a different genre.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There were plenty of normal large sharks around at the time. Again, just use Chasmus stats. Add an additional stat dot or 2 if you feel it necessary. There is no reason general Rokea need Megalodon kin. An not all Megalodons reached 60ft. A large great white Chasmus can already be 45ft long. that would seem to represent the species close enough. </div> </div> </div>You'd be hard-pressed to find a pointer long enough to get a Chasmus that size, and the proportions would be quite different. You might also still be five feet too small, in terms of both length and circumference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T22:12:01-08:00","id":790683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790677#post790677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would advise against using Hispo for a hypothetical dire wolf form's mechanics, since it's a wolf the size of a horse. Just take off all of the Lupus Dex bonus and add one to Strength; its running speed should be down around Crinos, too. Bite damage mods would increase, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree, I don't think that's what the OP is going for. Like I said, I don't see the actual need to do any of this, but am trying to come up with helpful suggestions anyway. Switching Dex to Str bonuses is also a possible solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790677#post790677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And in many cases, the &quot;ancestors&quot; cited aren't. Dire wolves were distant cousins to wolves at best, not their progenitors. Megalodon was a kind of a latecomer (but might have been an ancestor to the modern sand-tiger shark, under the <i>Carcharocles</i> hypothesis). Sabertooth cats didn't beget modern cats, big or small. It might work for the Mokole, given the size of <i>Deinosuchus</i>, but for other changers, their animal kin didn't really have remarkably huge progenitors. Giant Protoype Creatures are a thing from a different genre.</div> </div> </div> </div> And I agree with all of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790677#post790677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You'd be hard-pressed to find a pointer long enough to get a Chasmus that size, and the proportions would be quite different. You might also still be five feet too small, in terms of both length and circumference.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not all (or even many) Rokea of the time need to be huge. There is no reason the Rokea aren't going to be spread across species large and small. In fact, having bred with the smaller species pretty much ensures their survival and fulfills their purpose. Seems like the OP is just looking for a way to represent the larger shark species of the time, and so my suggestion was to just ignore Squamus stats and give them Chasmus stats. It certainly isn't a perfect solution. But I think its better than saying they get +5 to all physicals in their breed form and then can go Chasmus and Crinos on top of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:53:48-08:00","id":790957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790658#post790658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe there should be any &quot;primal ananasi&quot;. So for me, leaving the insect changers as is works out just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean this in that I was changing the stats of existing fera, I was proposing a what-if senario i which small numbers of the lost changing breeds and ancestors of the current ones(though distantly related) survived their &quot;Extinction&quot;(and adding stats to those NPC's). These &quot;Lost ones&quot; could be easily used as enemies(them feeling Gaia abandoned them when they needed her) or as allies(discovering and gathering up the lost tribes to give could be used before a massive battle or as a redemption story for the garou to regain the trust of the other fera after the wars of rage.)<br /> <br /> Besides I'm pretty sure the Insect breeds have existed even before the mokole (Ananasi being the only ones left) and considering how big insects used to get in the time before dinosaurs....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:54:29-08:00","id":791154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790957#post790957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mean this in that I was changing the stats of existing fera, I was proposing a what-if senario i which small numbers of the lost changing breeds and ancestors of the current ones(though distantly related) survived their &quot;Extinction&quot;(and adding stats to those NPC's). These &quot;Lost ones&quot; could be easily used as enemies(them feeling Gaia abandoned them when they needed her) or as allies(discovering and gathering up the lost tribes to give could be used before a massive battle or as a redemption story for the garou to regain the trust of the other fera after the wars of rage.)<br /> <br /> Besides I'm pretty sure the Insect breeds have existed even before the mokole (Ananasi being the only ones left) and considering how big insects used to get in the time before dinosaurs....</div> </div> </div> </div>Arthropods, please, of which insects are of but one example, and not the one that furnished spiders, trilobites, or sea scorpions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:18:02-08:00","id":791191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=791154#post791154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arthropods, please, of which insects are of but one example, and not the one that furnished spiders, trilobites, or sea scorpions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the era after the life in sea one, after the plants had filled the atmosphere with so much oxygen that it could support massive arthropods on land(including ancestors to the spider, centipede, moth, etc.), but I can't remember any of the important names for the major era's(I'm horrible with names in general)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:24:27-08:00","id":791224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=791191#post791191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant the era after the life in sea one, after the plants had filled the atmosphere with so much oxygen that it could support massive arthropods on land(including ancestors to the spider, centipede, moth, etc.), but I can't remember any of the important names for the major era's(I'm horrible with names in general)</div> </div> </div> </div>Carboniferous. The increased oxygen came with increased carbon-fixation, without the means to break it down, so we also got our fossil fuels from there.<br /> <br /> (and our radioactive fuels from the Mesozoic...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:53:30-08:00","id":791273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/789857-primal-fera?p=790957#post790957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides I'm pretty sure the Insect breeds have existed even before the mokole (Ananasi being the only ones left) and considering how big insects used to get in the time before dinosaurs....</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ananasi acknowledge that the Mokole and Rokea are older than themselves, at least as of their breed book. So I believe your timeline might be a bit off, at least according to canon. By all means, that shouldn't stop you from doing whatever you want with your own game.<br /> Having said that I realize that I don't necessarily agree with your view of what ancient Gaia was like so I am of limited help. I don't see the point (or even the appeal) of forcing all of the Breeds into having giant proto-ancestor versions of themselves. I suppose playing with the size factor might be something, but in the end those animals proved inferior to their more efficient relatives.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}